This code provides trainings & testings of IWSLT14 English-German, WMT14 English-German translation tasks

===============================
# Data format ./data/
- bpe.train.* bpe.valid.*, bpe.test.* is tokenized, BPE applied datasets given to model as inputs
- test.* is tokenized (not BPE applied) test references for tokenBLEU measurement
- ref.* is untokenized raw references for SacreBLEU measurement

===============================
# Required Python Packages
- torch
- numpy
- sacrebleu
- sacremoses
- neptune >= 1.2.0


==============================
# Process to run training
- Set training configurations in train_iwslt14_ende.sh (or train_wmt14_ende.sh)
--- Small Transformer for iwslt14_ende, Base Transformer for wmt14_ende as defaults

- bash train_iwslt14_ende.sh (GPU_IDs) (#_of_GPUs)
- bash train_wmt14_ende.sh (GPU_IDs) (#_of_GPUs)

e.g. single GPU training : bash train_iwslt14_ende.sh 0 1
     multi GPU training  : bash train_iwslt14_ende.sh 0,1,2 3


==============================
# Process to run testing
- Set testing configurations(e.g. beam_width, test_subdir name, sacrebleu_tokenizer, 
  lowercase sensitivity) in test_iwslt14_ende.sh (or test_wmt14_ende.sh)

- bash run_experiments.sh (GPU_ID) (TASK_NAME)
* GPU_ID : should be single GPU for testing
* TASK_NAME : 'iwslt14_ende' or 'wmt14_ende'

e.g. bash run_experiments.sh 0 iwslt14_ende


==============================
# descriptions of .py files
- Beam.py : source for beam search
- dataset.py : source for dataloadeer
                - dataloader is token-level (not batch-level) data iterator
                * It is implemented originally for various types of dataset (bilingual, monolingual)
- nmt_const.py : it contains special tokens' information
- nmt_ensemble.py : source for checkpoint_ensemble method. (nmt_main.py runs this ensemble code at
                    every validations)
- nmt_main.py : this is main code for training
                - (optional) Initialize Neptune project
                - Call model & optimizer
                - Run training iterations (forward model, backprop, update)
		--- update_step means the unit for regular update (for larger tokensize with small 
								   GPU)
		    e.g. update_step=1 means it updates at every iterations
			 update_step=2 means it updates at every second iterations
                - Run validations at every valid_iter
		* validation makes latest ensemble model everytime and save it if it shows the best 
		  performance
		WARNING: Note that the BLEU score of 'multi_validation' is not 100% correct.
- nmt_model_tm.py : source for Transformer model		
		- final loss is normalized by moving_averaged batchsize (model collects and computes
		  average batchsize at every iterations)
		- 'multi_validation' means the validation code for 'multi_validation' in 
		  nmt_trans.py . It adds paddings horizontally/vertically to make fixed-size outputs.
- nmt_run.py : this is main code for whole pipeline
		- when 'train' mode, 
		--- it makes new sub directory in /results which is a unique 
		    directory name (determined by configurations) for the new training. 
		    WARNING : if you run a new training with the same configuration, it will delete 
				the existing sub directory after 5 seconds.
		--- Load dataloaders from dataset.py
		--- run training main code of nmt_main.py
		- when 'test' mode
		--- Load configuration & model used for the training
		--- run 'Test_SacreBLEU' to get the valid SacreBLEU scores with true references 
			(and tokenized_references for tokenBLEU)
- nmt_trans.py : source codes for main of validation, testing
		- 'multi_validation' is used for validation during training, this is faster when use 
		  multi-GPU. 
		 WARNING: Its BLEU score is not 100% correct. It computes BLEU with target data 
			loaded from dataloader, not true reference)
		- 'Test_SacreBLEU' is used for testing. 
		
